# Line-ending policy.
#
# Added 2026-11-21 after `18_population_coverage/population_genotype_map.p` was found
# corrupted in the working tree: git's heuristic did not detect it as binary, so LF was
# converted to CRLF on checkout and 380,776 CRLF pairs were written into a pickle. The
# file became unloadable -- `collections\r.OrderedDict\r` -- and step23 aborted. The
# committed blob was still clean, so the file was restored from it.
#
# Pickles and the other formats below must never be line-ended. The data formats this
# project actually reads are listed explicitly rather than relying on auto-detection.

*.p         binary
*.pkl       binary
*.pickle    binary
*.npy       binary
*.npz       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.ckp.gz    binary
*.model.gz  binary
*.cache     binary

# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository. Git still checks them out with
# native endings on Windows; only the stored form is pinned.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.tsv       text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.fasta     text eol=lf
*.log       text eol=lf
